{#- The proof under an opening (the home hero and each inner page's), as credentials (25 October 2026,
    the user: "ICMR approved, patents granted in India and Japan etc ... need to be different visually
    ... to make them stand out without overwhelming the user"). A quiet row under the buttons, set
    apart by its marks rather than by boxes (so it never reads as more buttons): ICMR's approval a seal
    in life green, the patents the two countries' codes; anything else keeps its own icon. The three that can be checked link
    to where they are shown. items: [{ icon, text }], as the pages' front matter writes them; style is
    the opening's rise order (--i) on the home page.
    Import it with {% from "credentials.njk" import credentials %}. -#}
{%- macro credentials(items, classes, style) -%}
<ul class="hero-proof creds{{ ' ' + classes if classes }}"{% if style %} style="{{ style }}"{% endif %}>
  {%- for item in items %}
  {%- set count = item.text.split(" ")[0] %}
  {%- if item.text == "ICMR approved" %}
  <li class="cred cred-icmr"><a href="/technology/#approvals"><span class="cred-mark cred-seal">{% icon "badge-check" %}</span><span class="cred-text">{{ item.text }}</span></a></li>
  {%- elif "atent" in item.text and "India and Japan" in item.text %}
  <li class="cred cred-patent"><a href="/technology/#patents"><span class="cred-mark cred-codes cred-label" aria-hidden="true"><b>IN</b><b>JP</b></span><span class="cred-text">{{ item.text }}</span></a></li>
  {%- elif r/^\d+ sites/.test(item.text) %}
  <li class="cred cred-sites"><a href="/our-work/#sites"><span class="cred-mark cred-icon">{% icon "map-pin" %}</span><span class="cred-text">{{ item.text }}</span></a></li>
  {%- else %}
  <li class="cred"><span class="cred-mark cred-icon">{% icon item.icon %}</span><span class="cred-text">{{ item.text }}</span></li>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- endfor %}
</ul>
{%- endmacro %}
